        WALK (0x1), FLYING (0x2), OBJECT_COLLECT (0x4000), HAY_CART_RELATED
        (0x2000000) and UNK3 (0x8000000) have no writer in the client; they are
        only meaningful on packets the server sends.

    server -> client (STATE),
        NetAvatar::applyTankStateAndEvents @ 0x14050C560 (rdi = pkt) decodes the
        received flags (addresses in the 0x14050C6xx-0x14050CCxx range):

            bit 4  0x10        -> avatar+0x61 (facing left)
            bit 5  0x20        -> avatar+0xDC (on-ground)
            bit 6  0x40        -> NetAvatar::onBurn
            bit 7  0x80        -> NetAvatar::onJump
            bit 8  0x100       -> avatar pos = pkt.vector_x/vector_y then
                                  NetAvatar::onPositionSnapped
            bit 9  0x200       -> tile = getTileAt(pkt.int_x, pkt.int_y) ->
                                  HandleTileActionResult; if the local player's
                                  collision rect overlaps that tile ->
                                  NetAvatar::OnPunched(localPlayer, at, attacker)
                                  and the client sends GOT_PUNCHED (type 23)
            bit 10 0x400       -> tile -> bounceTileX/Y = int_x/int_y and
                                  bounceItemId = pkt.value + effect
                                  (sub_14012ECC0); unless a state block is
                                  pending (avatar+0x120) the client re-broadcasts
                                  PLACE|TILE_CHANGE by ORing its own event mask;
                                  a missing tile logs "All, hell naw"
            bit 11 0x800       -> (with bit 9: `test flags, 0x280`) audio effect
                                  sub_140118B10
            bit 12 0x1000      -> NetAvatar::onPunched (being-hit reaction)
            bit 13 0x2000      -> re-broadcasts RESPAWN|TILE_CHANGE; controller
                                  +0x8C = 1; sub_1404F7410 + respawn effect
            bit 14 0x4000      -> plays "audio/object_collect.wav"
            bit 15 0x8000      -> NetAvatar::onTileBounceHit(pkt.value, int_x,
                                  int_y)
            bit 16 0x10000     -> `test byte [pkt+0x0E], 1` -> onDamagingTile
            bit 17 0x20000     -> avatar+0xDD (slide)
            bit 18 0x40000     -> avatar+0xDF (slow-fall A / parasol)
            bit 19 0x80000     -> avatar+0xE0 (slow-fall B / glide)
            bit 21 0x200000    -> wall-hang effect; else if avatar+0x2088 == 0x14
                                  -> avatar+0x2088 = 2
            bit 22 0x400000    -> pet axis + handlePunchDisplayEffectAndSfx
            bit 23 0x800000    -> pet axis + local OnPunched + send GOT_PUNCHED
            bit 24 0x1000000   -> pet axis += 1 while effective < 3
            bit 26 0x4000000   -> avatar+0xE1 (double-jump animation)
            bit 28 0x10000000  -> NetAvatar::onAcidBurn

        no handler was found for bits 0, 1, 2, 20, 25, 27 in this function
        (bit 2 is handled by applyTankStatePacket instead, below).

        NetAvatar::applyTankStatePacket @ 0x1404F58C0 (the avatar+0x10 network
        state block) copies pkt+0x04..0x34 into avatar+0x10..0x47 first, then
        tests `byte [pkt+0x0C] & 4` (RESET_VISUAL_STATE): when set, the snapshot
        is copied into the visual block avatar+0x80..+0xB7, avatar+0x1C |= 4 and
        the render position snaps to avatar+0x98/0x9C; when clear the visual
        block is rebuilt from the avatar via fillTankStatePacket.

    forced-send mask (0x10C16740),
        sendTankState force-sends the frame (bypassing the body memcmp) whenever
        `pkt.flags & 0x10C16740 != 0` (0x1404F5F30). the mask is exactly ten
        one-shot bits:
            0x40 FIRE_DAMAGE           0x4000 OBJECT_COLLECT
            0x100 GOT_KILLED           0x10000 DAMAGE
            0x200 PUNCH                0x400000 POWER_UP_PUNCH_START
            0x400 PLACE                0x800000 POWER_UP_PUNCH_END
            0x2000 RESPAWN             0x10000000 ACID_DAMAGE
        TILE_CHANGE (0x800) and GOT_PUNCHED (0x1000) are NOT in the mask. an
        action frame leaves immediately because avatar+0x134 & 0x800
        (TILE_CHANGE) resets the 200 ms poll timer at the top of sendTankState
        (0x1404F5E4C).

    per-type flags,
        TILE_CHANGE_REQUEST (3): sendTileChangeRequest @ 0x140407570 sets
            FACING_LEFT (0x10) from the local player's facing (0x14040760F);
            value/int_x/int_y carry the item and the target tile, vector_x/y the
            position stamp. no other flags.
        CALL_FUNCTION (1), SEND_LOCK (15), NPC, PET_BATTLE, SELECT_TILE_INDEX:
            EXTENDED (0x8) means extended_data follows at pkt+0x38.
            tankGetExtended @ 0x14053F9D0 returns pkt+0x38 iff the bit is set;
            SendPacketRaw @ 0x140541BF0 appends pkt->extended_len bytes when it
            is (0x140541C5D); readers: ProcessTankUpdatePacket (many sites),
            handleNPC, handlePetBattle, handleSelectTileIndex, handleSendLock,
            sub_1403F29C0, sub_1403F43E0.
        GOT_PUNCHED (23), APP_CHECK_RESPONSE (24), APP_INTEGRITY_FAIL (25):
            the flag word is zero / unused (the app-check hash and the integrity
            code live in `value`).
        NETWORLD_SNAPSHOT player records: the per-player `flags` field is a
            TankFlags dword (samples above show FACING_LEFT, STANDING,
            DOUBLE_JUMPED); it is kept in the 12-slot snapshot ring and used
            during interpolation.

    unknowns,
        - WALK/FLYING/HAY_CART_RELATED/UNK3: no client writer or consumer found
          in this pass.
        - SWIM is written by the client but has no receive handler in
          applyTankStateAndEvents.
        - the exact triggers of sub_1404FF6C0 / sub_140500110 / sub_140500A70
          (all `0x1800`/`0x2800` re-broadcast-style writers) are not classified.

